{"base_rate":0.5588673621460507,"brier":0.22065484351713857,"bss":0.10497425765765778,"bss_hi":0.18101089674450194,"bss_lo":0.018012460282808212,"chart":{"base":[786.7,72.2],"fp":[350.3,308.7],"lead":"62,310.3 272,309.1 482,307.3 692,300.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.10 — higher than 18% of cities","fp":"low end +14pp, high end +14pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.5 °C — better than 100% of cities","rel":"promised 14% → rained 26%; promised 98% → rained 81%"},"rel":"152.2,353.9 321.7,285.2 479.5,226 595.1,153.5 678.2,114"},"country":"AG","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10417287630402383,"ess":481.7195434428139,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Saint John&#x27;s</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Saint John&#x27;s rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(7%), there is still roughly a <b>23%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 671 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 6.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.10, ranked 175 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(152&ndash;185) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>50</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Saint John&#x27;s</b> <span class=\"muted\">Antigua and Barbuda</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.10</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>152&ndash;185\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>671 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Saint John&#x27;s &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days s